From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: sun50i-h616: Fix audio PLL sigma-delta table rates

ccu_nm_set_rate() scales the requested rate by the fixed post-divider
before it searches the sigma-delta table, and ccu_nm_recalc_rate()
divides the table rate by it afterwards, so the table has to hold the
rate before the post-divider - as the A64 and H6 tables do. The H616
table holds the rate after it: 24 MHz * 40.96 / 5 is 196.608 MHz, not
98.304 MHz.

The result is a PLL that runs at twice the rate the clock framework
believes. A request for 49.152 MHz - what the audio hub now asks for via
pll-audio-2x, since the divider code was converted to
divider_determine_rate() - matches the 98304000 entry, programs the
sigma-delta settings and produces 98.304 MHz. HDMI audio then plays at
double speed and underruns.

Store the rates before the post-divider. The exact 24.576 MHz path for
the audio hub becomes pll-audio-1x with the PLL at 98.304 MHz, which is
the only exact candidate and therefore the one the divider code picks.

Fixes: d0c322b6e4bf ("clk: sunxi-ng: h616: Add sigma-delta modulation settings for audio PLL")
Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
@@ -223,8 +223,8 @@
  */
 
 static struct ccu_sdm_setting pll_audio_sdm_table[] = {
-	{ .rate = 90316800, .pattern = 0xc001288d, .m = 3, .n = 22 },
-	{ .rate = 98304000, .pattern = 0xc001eb85, .m = 5, .n = 40 },
+	{ .rate = 180633600, .pattern = 0xc001288d, .m = 3, .n = 22 },
+	{ .rate = 196608000, .pattern = 0xc001eb85, .m = 5, .n = 40 },
 };
 
 #define SUN50I_H616_PLL_AUDIO_REG	0x078
